---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Content policy"
  description="What B2BRated publishes, what it will not publish, and how to ask us to correct or remove something."
  path="/content-policy"
>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>
    Category comparisons, product pages and guides written by us. Facts about a product, such as prices, plan limits
    and contract terms, come from the vendor's own pages and link back to them. Our own commentary is labelled as ours.
    The <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> explains how we choose and check what goes on a page.
  </p>

  <h2>What we will not publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices, features or claims we could not read on a public vendor page or in a written quote.</li>
    <li>Invented reviews, ratings, customers or testimonials.</li>
    <li>Paid placements that look like editorial content.</li>
    <li>Copied text from vendors, review sites or other publishers.</li>
    <li>Other people's private data, threats, harassment or hate speech.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reviews and other user content</h2>
  <p>
    Reviews are not open yet. When they open, only signed-in users can write them, and every review must follow the
    <a href="/review-guidelines">review guidelines</a>. We may remove content that breaks those rules, and we say why when
    we do.
  </p>

  <h2>Report a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If something on the site is wrong, out of date or should not be there, write to
    <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" /> with the page address and what is wrong. For a factual error,
    include a link to a public page that shows the correct fact. We read every report, change what the evidence supports,
    and tell you if we disagree. See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for the full process.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of our content</h2>
  <p>
    You may quote short passages with a link back to the page. Copying whole pages or republishing our comparisons is not
    allowed without written permission. The <a href="/terms">terms</a> cover the details.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
